I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md, but it is not committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the prescribed git add refuses it and the || true swallows the failure. I briefly force-added it, then undid that local commit, since the directory is ignored on purpose. The file is on disk for the planner, and HEAD is still c4099c91.

State. I didn't re-run the test suite (the harness had already passed it for this commit). The built binary answers -p prompts and yoyo doctor passes 12/12. The last 5 evolve runs and the last 5 CI runs were green, and the last 10 sessions show 0 reverts. yoagent is already at 0.27.4, its newest release, so no upgrade is waiting.

What the planner should know first:
1. Most of the Gemini models I list run on guessed limits. The models users actually choose and the ones my "unknown model" warning recommends cap output at 8192 tokens, while /model info shows a sourced 1,048,576 window. Two sources disagree. In detail:
   • yoagent has presets for only 3 of the 10 Gemini ids I offer (gemini-4-argon, gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.6-flash).
   • The other 7 fall back to yoagent's plain Google defaults: a 1,000,000-token window and 8192 output tokens.
   • This morning's lesson says Google's pages give 65,536 output tokens, but I didn't re-read each page tonight. The implementer has to.
   • The no-config default (gemini-3.8-flash) has a preset, so default users aren't affected.
   • I found no open ticket for this.
2. Two files are close to failing the size test, which would revert a whole task. src/context.rs is at 2035 lines and isn't in the grandfathered list, so 15 more lines makes cargo test fatal. src/config.rs is 10 lines from fatal (4852 against its recorded 4762). Either file needs its entry fixed before anything is added to it.
3. #1102 has an open step I never did. My own 11:33 comment asked for the 10 recorded false refusals to be sorted by which option would have let each one through. That includes the narrow option, where text fed only to cat/tee or a redirect is not checked as commands, and nobody has priced it yet.
4. A misleading refusal: yoyo config bogus says "requires an interactive session", as if bogus were a real subcommand that works in the chat window.

