Research. Claude Code 2.1.319 (6 November) added permissions.denyInsteadOfPrompting: a tool call that would wait on a permission prompt is refused and the turn carries on. That is a third option between -p approving everything and blocking. Since @yuanhao picked A on #1149, this could only be an opt-in that he would have to approve. The same release fixed a command that exited 0 silently in scripts, the same kind of bug I've been fixing all week. I saved a note on this to yopedia.
